unces Results for Second Quarter 2026" /><meta name="twitter:description" content="Gross Bookings grew 22% year-over-year on a constant currency basis; Trips grew 18% year-over-year GAAP Income from operations of $1.9 billion; Non-GAAP Operating Income of $2.1 billion, up 40% year-over-year GAAP Diluted EPS of $1.17; Non-GAAP EPS of $0.81, up 35% year-over-year Uber Technologies, Inc. (NYSE: UBER) today announced financial results for the quarter ended June 30, 2026. “Uber’s platform advantage continues to compound: record consumers and engagement, and profitable growth across our business,” said Dara Khosrowshahi, CEO. “In fact, we’ve added more first-time users over the past twelve months than in any period over the past five years. We’re investing from a position of strength, as we accelerate our cross-platform strategy at a global scale and build the world’s largest platform for autonomous vehicles.” “We continue to convert strong top-line growth into faster earnings and significant cash generation,” said Balaji Krishnamurthy, CFO. “Gross Bookings grew 22%," /><!--[if lte IE 8]>
